# THIS TREE IS NEW, AND THE CONFIG STILL APPLIES TO CHANGED LINES ONLY.
#
# basalt checks changed lines because it acquired its config after 26,000 lines
# were already written and a whole-tree reformat would have produced a diff
# nobody could audit. Umbra has no such history: every line here was written
# under this file, so a whole-file check would pass today.
#
# It is still a changed-lines check, for a reason that outlives the migration
# argument. clang-format's output is not stable across major versions -- the
# CI lane pins one, contributors have whatever their distribution ships -- and
# under a whole-file check a version skew reformats files the change never
# touched, so the diff under review stops being the change. Restricting the
# check to the lines a commit actually edits bounds that damage to the lines
# their author was already looking at. The lane prints its clang-format version
# for the same reason; see .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# ReflowComments is OFF. With it on, editing one line inside a comment block
# rewraps the block around it, and a one-line change arrives as a twelve-line
# diff through paragraphs the author never read. The comments in this repo carry
# the reasoning and are the part most worth reviewing; they must not churn.
BasedOnStyle: Google
Language: Cpp
Standard: c++17
ColumnLimit: 80
IndentWidth: 2
AccessModifierOffset: -1
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Left
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
ReflowComments: false
